{"title": "Reproduce evidence handoffs copying whole histories", "goal": "Reproduce on main that a successor task's handoff copies its predecessor's whole evidence folder, including earlier tasks' evidence, so repeats pile up under the evidence retention rules; trace where the copy happens.", "userWords": "a user report of infinitary repeatedly copy the same files causing a lot of disk used - can we investigate?\n\na Rust project accumulated tens of gigabytes of duplicate test evidence even after completed tasks’ working copies and temporary folders were removed.\n\nThe duplicated files were not compiled binaries or ordinary build outputs.\n\nThey were predominantly JSON reference-test recordings: complete simulation states before and after actions, memory, results/errors, events, clocks and random-state diagnostics. \n\nThe handoff procedure required each successor task to copy its predecessor’s complete evidence set into a fresh evidence folder.\n\nBecause the predecessor already contained earlier tasks’ evidence, each handoff copied the accumulated history again, while older folders remained retained.\n\nRust did not create these copies; the development handoff tooling did.\n\nThe Rust program and its native tests use checked-in code and fixtures; these larger raw recordings belong to the separate development-evidence workflow.\n\nCleaning Rust build outputs does not clean that external evidence store, and merging code does not expire it.\n\nThe task system correctly removed the audited working copies and temporary folders, but retained evidence under a different rule.\n\nEvidence waits seven days after task closure and can remain longer when another open task names it as its basis.\n\nThat hold can cover an entire evidence folder even when the successor task has not started.\n\nThe historical audit measured 76.97 GB of evidence allocation: 61.85 GB of recorded repeats, 13.60 GB counted once, and 1.52 GB unclassified.\n[truncated 0 more characters; full text: ~/Library/Application Support/infinitary/overflow/pasted-text-e8afa600.txt]", "constraints": "read-only; free: Read the whole pasted report at ~/Library/Application Support/infinitary/overflow/pasted-text-e8afa600.txt before acting. Do not touch the user's real evidence stores; use a scratch home.", "expectedKind": "reproduce", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1009 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
