{"title": "Investigate why INF-1191 stalled before its final push", "goal": "Explain with evidence how INF-1191 (task f7dff524) sat about 5 hours without pushing after the captain chose merge. It had brought its branch up to date and started its tests. Also propose concrete ways to prevent or detect such a stall.", "userWords": "i want an independent investigation for how such a stall could happen, and how do we prevent it", "constraints": "read-only; free: Context: the captain clicked merge on INF-1191 (task f7dff524, runs on the Mac mini). The merge stopped because the branch had to be brought up to date with main. The crewmate did that and started its tests (a background run), planning to push once they passed. It never returned to push, and no PR existed for about 5 hours, until the first mate steered it. Trace from the task's record and session, the host's code (the Infinitary repo, or the packaged self-source at /Applications/Infinitary.app/Contents/Resources/self-source, starting from self-map.json, which must not be modified) and logs. Find what should have woken the crewmate or the first mate when the background job finished or went quiet, and why nothing did. Propose prevention and detection, with the one you would pick as the default.", "expectedKind": "research", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1244 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
