{"title": "Assess whether PR merge logic is too rigid in the host", "goal": "Analyze the recent fixes, and the backlog, that couple pull request merges and checks to task lifecycle. Judge whether the current host-side logic is too rigid and not \"bitter lesson pilled\" enough. Weigh moving merge handling into tools plus instructions, taking INF-1177's plan into account, and answer with a recommended direction.", "userWords": "we recently fixed / improved quite a few things related to PR merge/check's coupling with task lifecycle. i think there's a few in the backlog as well. i want to take a step back to assess whether our system is too rigid here. have a fable crewmate analyze what happened and whether our current logic is not \"bitter lesson pilled\" enough. i'm wondering whether PR merge should be turned into tools + instructions instead of a lot of app host side logic. this analysis should take INF-1177's plan into considerations as well", "constraints": "read-only; free: Read INF-1177's plan in full. Survey the recently merged fixes and the open backlog tasks about merges, checks, holds and task lifecycle (for example INF-1342, INF-1263's cancelled-run red check, and the check_change diagnosis tasks). Note which failures came from rigid host rules and which came from real safety needs, and say what must stay enforced by the host, such as consent and merge permission.", "expectedKind": "research", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1347 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
