{"title": "Find why the card's merge button would not merge", "goal": "Explain, with evidence from the app's code and records, why the \"Merge with the phone check red\" button on card card-fm-65-2a298a (task e065dd46, PR #497) showed \"This action changed or still waits for other work. Read its current card before confirming.\" and did not merge, even after the captain's override of the checks, rerun, asks-first and story holds.", "userWords": "independently investigate why the merge button couldn't work on the last card", "constraints": "read-only; free: Facts to start from: the first mate made the card with a settle merge effect on task e065dd46 (INF-1266) and revised it three times in place. The captain saw the message above instead of a working button, twice: before and after the first mate recorded overrides of the checks and rerun holds. The first mate's own settle_task merge-pr was refused, first for asks-first, then with 'The current story and all evidence must be published and read back before the completion card or merge', even after an override of the story hold. Trace each refusal to its code and records, say whether the button and the first mate's merge are blocked by the same gate, and whether the card revisions themselves made the click stale. The app's packaged source is at /Applications/Infinitary.app/Contents/Resources/self-source (start from self-map.json); read it only, never modify it.", "expectedKind": "research", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1363 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
{"title": "Find why PR #497 undid the phone-check budget", "goal": "Explain with evidence, step by step, how the captain's INF-1258 pick (\"Let a crewmate's phone check on request run only the parts its change touches\", plus \"start the picked instead of only filing them\") became INF-1266 (task e065dd46) and PR #497. PR #497 makes pull requests run every phone-check part with --full and deletes the part-time steps behind the 6-minute budget. Name exactly which step introduced each departure from the captain's words.", "userWords": "that was a big screw up, right? it did the exact opposite of what i asked?? investigate exactly what caused it", "constraints": "read-only; free: Trace each link in the chain with evidence, and quote each actor's exact words: - the INF-1258 nightly audit's finding text and its card; - the captain's choice and write-in; - the first mate's spawn of INF-1266 (its goal, user_words and constraints); - the crewmate's own brief; - its plan or report; - the PR #497 diff that removes the part-time steps and adds --full. For each one, say whether it matches the captain's words, narrows them, or contradicts them. Also say whether INF-1343's budget pick (INF-1346, PR #528) came before or after INF-1266's spawn, and whether anything told INF-1266 about it. The app's own source is at /Applications/Infinitary.app/Contents/Resources/self-source. Start from self-map.json there if you need to see how a spawn goal becomes a brief, and read it only; never modify it. On the card, give a plain verdict on the captain's question. List the concrete causes and the fixes they suggest, then offer filing those fixes as the default action.", "expectedKind": "retrieval", "lane": "quick", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1366 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
{"title": "Count real problems vs flakes in recent phone checks", "goal": "Count the recent failed iPhone and iPad phone-check runs on Infinitary pull requests and main, and sort each into a real problem the change caused or a flaky test. Show the evidence for each, the time the failures cost, and which flaky journeys come up most.", "userWords": "recently failed phone checks seem to have slowed a lot of things down. how many of the failures were legit problems caught, vs flaky tests?", "constraints": "read-only; free: Cover roughly the last two weeks of native-phone check runs. Count a failure as real only when evidence shows the change caused it: a fix commit followed, or the same failure doesn't appear on main or on unrelated PRs. Count it as flaky when it passed on a rerun with the same code, or the same journey failed on unrelated PRs or main. Mark everything else not established. Count runner or infrastructure failures separately. Name the flake tasks that already cover the recurring journeys, such as INF-1338, INF-1263, INF-1371 and INF-1251, and point out any recurring flake no task covers, such as the iPad address keyboard-focus failure. Start no reruns.", "expectedKind": "research", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1374 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
{"title": "Explain the uneven crewmate spacing on the orbit", "goal": "Explain why the crewmates in the captain's screenshot of the crew scene look unevenly spaced around the orbit. Work out whether it is the intended two-orbit layout, perspective or tilt, a seating bug, or something else, and say which window or app it is. Answer with drawn figures, and give the code reasons and a fix only if it is a bug.", "userWords": "why it seems the crewmates aren't evenly distributed on the orbit here?", "constraints": "read-only; free: Look at the screenshot at the path in the captain's words. The desktop's growing two-orbit ring was just brought to iOS in PR #517 (INF-1331, task 7af96458), so check the seating and orbit code on both desktop and iOS. Compare the seat angles the code computes for the crewmate count you see in the screenshot with where the crewmates actually appear.", "expectedKind": "retrieval", "lane": "quick", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1375 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
{"title": "Why crewmates find no model key after upgrading", "goal": "Find the likely causes, ranked with evidence from the code, of a user's crewmates all failing after an upgrade with \"No API key found for the selected model\" while the first mate works and the Intelligence tab shows healthy sign-ins. Say what the user can check or do for each cause, and whether it is a bug to fix.", "userWords": "a user is reporting that after upgrading to infinitary, his first mate works, but crewmates all stopped working despite the intelligence tab shows the sign-ins are good. his own claude code and codex etc in terminals are also working fine. what possible cause could be causing this problem in infinitary?", "constraints": "read-only; free: Read both screenshots at the paths in the captain's words first. The error comes from the crew's engine (pi-coding-agent inside app.asar). Trace how the crew's engine gets credentials for each provider compared with the first mate: credential handoff, the migration from the earlier app (Firstmate 3000) to Infinitary, the config or home folder the engine reads, and how model ids are mapped. Check whether the model being unavailable while still in the crew's medium slot points to an outdated model catalogue or model pins. Don't touch any real Keychain and don't print any secret.", "expectedKind": "research", "lane": "deep", "provenance": {"kind": "task-excerpt", "source": "INF-1380 task brief, words scrubbed; step lines relayed under the old guidance left out"}}
